# Turn the Node version requirement from advice into a refusal.
#
# `engines` alone only warns, and the warning is the problem: a Node 20 install
# printed 17 EBADENGINE lines and then BUILT ANYWAY, producing a `.next` that
# grove-webapp.service (which runs Node 22) would go on to serve. Build and
# runtime disagreed while every step reported success — the failure this repo's
# stale-surface rules exist to catch, wearing a warning instead of an error.
#
# Trade-off, stated because it will surprise someone: this enforces EVERY
# package's `engines`, not just ours, so a future transitive dep that demands a
# Node newer than yours becomes a hard install failure rather than a warning.
# That is the intended direction — an unbuildable tree should say so — but the
# fix is to move Node forward, not to delete this line.
engine-strict=true
